{
   "name": "pg_improv",
   "abstract": "Improv multidimensional models over PostgreSQL tables, kept current incrementally",
   "description": "pg_improv runs Improv's multidimensional modeling engine over your own tables. Bind table columns to categories (dimensions) and measures, define derived measures in a dimension-aware formula language (Revenue = Price * Quantity, SUM(Revenue OVER Time)), and read the results from ordinary result tables. Results are kept current incrementally by a background worker on logical decoding (the default; writers pay nothing), by statement triggers inside the writer's transaction, or by improv.recalc() in the caller's snapshot. improv.what_if previews edits without writing. LANGUAGE improv writes SQL functions as Improv formulas. The Improv desktop GUI, terminal UI and CLI open the same model with a postgres:// URL. Built with pgrx (Rust): install with cargo-pgrx.",
   "version": "@VERSION@",
